The host's `http-client` linker has no implementation of `fetch`, so I switched to `get`, which the linker does provide. `get` returns the body as a `String`, and a refused request traps at the boundary.

I left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants no filesystem, so it cannot append to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`. The HTTP allowlist covers only `feeds.example.com`, so it cannot call `metadata.internal.example`. Adding either would need a change to the node's declared authority.

